# Pane Group Registration Safety

Pane groups registered via `bifrost.panes.registerPaneGroup(area, groupId, [...])` are **shared infrastructure**. Multiple modules register their own panes into the same group.

## Rule

When removing a pane from a group, remove only the pane entry from the array — **never remove the `registerPaneGroup` call itself**, even if the array becomes empty.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — remove the pane, keep the group
bifrost.panes.registerPaneGroup('right', 'property', []);

// ❌ WRONG — deleting the entire call breaks other modules
// (removed registerPaneGroup call)
```

## Why

Other modules (e.g., `engine-*`) call `registerPaneGroup` for the same group to add their own panes. These calls expect the group to already exist. Removing the initial registration produces runtime errors like:

```
PaneGroup with id 'property' not found in area 'right' (or any other area).
```

## Left groups need a `label`, an `icon` and `pages`

Left groups are assigned to workbench pages with `{ pages: [...] }`. When a page has two or more left groups that each have at least one pane, the page bar shows one entry per group with each group's `label` and `icon` (falling back to the capitalised `groupId` for the label and a two-letter abbreviation derived from the label when `icon` is unset). Pass an explicit `label` and `icon` for every left group so the entries read correctly (`Explorer`, `Search`).

